SUMMARY:A Day in the Life of a Pathologist: The Science That Shapes Health
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260626T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260626T130000
DTSTAMP:20260611T121101Z
UID:9f720d950325ee3e45edba071a592333@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: General\\n\\nVisit the Grainger Science Hu
 b and meet scientists from the College of American Pathologists to  explo
 re the role of a pathologist and examine its impact on overall health. Thi
 s interactive drop-in experience will introduce the world of pathology thr
 ough hands-on observation\, pattern recognition\, and diagnostic thinking.
  Visitors will rotate through stations that mirror the work pathologists d
 o every day: examining tissues\, identifying disease patterns\, comparing 
 healthy and abnormal samples\, and using clues to determine diagnoses. Dis
 cover how pathology is the “detective work” of medicine\, combining sc
 ience\, visual analytics\, and classification to understand disease. Pleas
 e be advised that this Meet a Scientist session will feature human remains
 . Visitor discretion is advised.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.o
 rg/our-events/meet-a-scientist/a-day-in-the-life-of-a-pathologist-the-scie
 nce-that-shapes-health
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/a-day-in-the-l
 ife-of-a-pathologist-the-science-that-shapes-health
